    "narrative": "The centerpiece of today\u2019s lineup is **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 85.94 against Tomoyuki Sugano. Between the favorable hitting environment, the high-upside matchup against a soft xERA, and his vital role as a catalyst in the #2 spot, **Corbin Carroll** is our mandatory cornerstone. He is joined in the \"Elite\" tier by **Josh Naylor** (73.26) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17). **Josh Naylor**\u2019s high efficiency stems from an excellent +19% boost derived from the matchup against Walker Buehler, while **Gabriel Moreno** benefits from park factors and a vulnerable opposing arm, cementing them as our primary engines for R and RBI production today.\n\nStrategic lineup construction relies heavily on capitalizing on platoon and park advantages, even in volatile \"Lineup Pending\" scenarios. **Mickey Moniak** (68.88) provides significant value today despite the platoon disadvantage, as the park factors and SP matchup outweigh the negative dynamic platoon hit. Conversely, we are keeping **Austin Riley** on the bench with a 50.79 score; while he is a high-pedigree talent, the optimizer favored the higher projected efficiency and specific lineup placement of **Kyle Karros** (60.77). **Kyle Karros**\u2019s ability to leverage a +14% park boost ultimately edged out **Austin Riley** for the final infield spot. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that nearly every player is currently listed with a \"Lineup Pending\" status, introducing potential for late-game volatility. **Tyler Soderstrom** sits at a marginal 53.70, largely hampered by a -19% penalty against the low-xERA Trevor McDonald; should official lineups shuffle him further down the order or expose him to a pinch-hit risk, he remains the most likely candidate to be swapped for **Zach McKinstry** if the bench environment shifts. With **Jose Caballero** still sidelined on the IL, we are managing our remaining depth carefully to preserve game caps, specifically monitoring **Brice Turang** and **Trevor Story** to ensure their offensive output remains consistent with their mid-range projections.",
